  <h1>SpendBook Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p class="updated">
    Effective date: 29 October 2026<br>
    Last updated: 29 October 2026
  </p>

  <p>
    SpendBook is a personal expense-tracking application designed to help
    users record, organize, and review their income and expenses.
    This Privacy Policy explains how information is accessed, used,
    stored, and protected when you use SpendBook.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Developer:</strong> Shubham Rawat<br>
    <strong>Contact email:</strong> shivamrawat829@gmail.com
  </p>

  <h2>1. How SpendBook Works</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook is designed to work offline without requiring users to
    create an account or register with the developer. Expense records
    are intended to be stored locally on your device. Optional Pro
    features are available through in-app purchases processed by Google Play.
  </p>

  <p>
    Google Play processes purchase-related information as necessary for
    billing. The app's actual data practices may also depend on Android
    backups, enabled device services, and the third-party libraries
    included in the app.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>

  <p>
    Depending on the features you use, SpendBook may store information
    you enter, including:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Expense and income amounts.</li>
    <li>Transaction dates and descriptions.</li>
    <li>Expense categories and notes.</li>
    <li>Payment methods, if entered.</li>
    <li>Budgets, summaries, and spending reports.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This information is used to provide expense tracking, categorization,
    budgeting, and reporting features. These records are intended to
    remain in the app's local storage and are not intentionally sent
    to a developer-operated cloud service as part of its offline functionality.
  </p>

  <p>
    Device backups, exported files, or other services enabled on your
    device may create copies outside the app's local storage.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Bank and SMS Transaction Access</h2>

  <p>
    If the SMS transaction recognition feature is included and enabled,
    SpendBook may request access to supported financial transaction
    messages to identify relevant transaction details.
  </p>

  <p>Depending on the message format, this may include:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Transaction amount and currency.</li>
    <li>Transaction date or time.</li>
    <li>Debit or credit status.</li>
    <li>Merchant or transaction description.</li>
    <li>Masked account or card references, if available and needed.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This information is used to help identify and record eligible
    transactions. The app must not access unrelated messages or use
    financial SMS information for advertising or unrelated purposes.
  </p>

  <p>
    SMS access is optional where manual expense entry is available.
    You may deny or revoke permission, although automatic transaction
    recognition may then be unavailable.
  </p>

  <p>
    SMS features are subject to Android and Google Play permission
    requirements. An expense-tracking use case does not automatically
    qualify an app for restricted SMS permissions.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How Information Is Used</h2>

  <p>Information processed by SpendBook is used to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Record and organize expenses and income.</li>
    <li>Identify supported financial transactions.</li>
    <li>Display summaries, budgets, and reports.</li>
    <li>Calculate spending totals and categories.</li>
    <li>Enable Pro features after a valid purchase.</li>
    <li>Provide the app's intended functionality.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    SpendBook is not intended to sell users' financial records or use
    financial SMS content for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data Storage and Transmission</h2>

  <p>
    Expense records and transaction details are intended to be stored
    locally on your device. SpendBook does not require an account or
    provide developer-operated cloud synchronization as part of the
    offline functionality described in this policy.
  </p>

  <p>
    Pro purchases are processed through Google Play. The app may receive
    purchase information needed to determine whether Pro features are
    available.
  </p>

  <p>
    The actual handling of information also depends on the app's
    implementation and included libraries. Any analytics, crash-reporting,
    advertising, remote verification, or other component that collects or
    transmits information must be accurately disclosed.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Pro Features and In-App Purchases</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook offers optional paid Pro features through Google Play's
    in-app billing system.
  </p>

  <p>
    Google Play processes payments according to its own terms and
    privacy practices. SpendBook does not directly collect or store
    your complete payment-card details.
  </p>

  <p>
    Depending on the billing implementation, the app may process
    purchase-related information such as product details, purchase
    status, transaction identifiers, or purchase tokens to enable
    and manage Pro features.
  </p>

  <p>
    Purchasing Pro does not, by itself, require a SpendBook account
    or enable cloud synchronization.
  </p>

  <p>
    For more information about Google's privacy practices, visit
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
      Google's Privacy Policy
    </a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Sharing of Information</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook's offline expense-tracking functionality is designed not
    to share locally stored financial records with the developer or
    unrelated third parties.
  </p>

  <p>
    Information may be processed by Google Play for purchases. Device
    backups, exported files, or sharing actions initiated by you may
    also place copies outside the app.
  </p>

  <p>
    SpendBook does not sell personal financial information. Any
    additional third-party collection, sharing, or transmission
    introduced by the app or its libraries must be disclosed accurately.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Permissions and Your Choices</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook requests permissions needed for its available features.
    If SMS access is requested, the app must explain its purpose and
    obtain any required consent before requesting the Android permission.
  </p>

  <p>
    You can deny or revoke permissions in your Android device settings.
    Features that depend on a denied permission may not work.
    Manual expense tracking remains available where supported.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>

  <p>
    Expense records are intended to remain on your device until you
    delete them, clear the app's stored data, or uninstall the app.
    Use the deletion controls provided by SpendBook, where available,
    to delete individual records or other stored information.
  </p>

  <p>
    Uninstalling the app generally removes its local application data,
    subject to Android behavior, device backups, exported files, and
    copies maintained by other services.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you export data or use device backup services, those copies may
    need to be deleted separately. SpendBook does not require a user
    account in the described setup, so there is no SpendBook account
    to delete.
  </p>

  <p>
    Purchase records retained by Google Play or other billing systems
    are subject to their respective policies and applicable legal requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data Security</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook is designed to keep expense records on your device and
    limit access to the app's intended functionality.
  </p>

  <p>
    We recommend keeping your device updated, using a secure screen
    lock, and taking care when exporting or sharing financial records.
    No storage method can guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook is not specifically designed to collect personal
    information from children. If the app is directed to children or
    knowingly processes children's personal information, additional
    privacy laws and Google Play requirements may apply.
  </p>

  <h2>12. International Users</h2>

  <p>
    SpendBook may be used in different countries. Privacy and
    data-protection requirements vary by jurisdiction. The developer
    will handle information in accordance with applicable laws.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

  <p>
    This Privacy Policy may be updated when SpendBook's features,
    data practices, or legal requirements change. The latest version
    will be published at the same public URL with an updated date.
  </p>

